import{_ as i,o as t,c as n,a2 as o}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const p=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 948 | Anti-Predation Heavenly-Dao Rules · Rule 14 | Observe-First-Then-Limited-Intervene","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 948 | Anti-Predation Heavenly-Dao Rules · Rule 14 | Observe-First-Then-Limited-Intervene","no":948,"module":5,"tags":["Heavenly-Dao Rule","Rule 14","Observe First","Limited Intervention","Causal Self-Discipline"],"related":["28-Cross-Plane Anchor Connection","916-Observe-First-Then-Limited-Intervene","947-Strict Cross-Plane-Operation Reporting"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0948_模块5-规则十四-先观测后有限干涉.md","filePath":"en/0948_模块5-规则十四-先观测后有限干涉.md"}'),r={name:"en/0948_模块5-规则十四-先观测后有限干涉.md"};function a(s,e,l,u,c,h){return t(),n("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[o('<h1 id="entry-948-anti-predation-heavenly-dao-rules-·-rule-14-observe-first-then-limited-intervene" tabindex="-1">Entry 948 | Anti-Predation Heavenly-Dao Rules · Rule 14 | Observe-First-Then-Limited-Intervene <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-948-anti-predation-heavenly-dao-rules-·-rule-14-observe-first-then-limited-intervene" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 948 | Anti-Predation Heavenly-Dao Rules · Rule 14 | Observe-First-Then-Limited-Intervene&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 5 · Civilization Final-Finalization Canonical Entries | Benchmark base: Document 28 | Series: Complete Collection of Anti-Predation Heavenly-Dao Rules</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-see-clearly-first-then-touch-gently" tabindex="-1">Introduction: see clearly first, then touch gently <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-see-clearly-first-then-touch-gently" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: see clearly first, then touch gently&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Rule 13 governs &quot;whether cross-plane needs reporting&quot;; Rule 14 governs &quot;after reporting, how to act appropriately.&quot; Heavenly-Dao rules give an extremely restrained answer: observe first, then limited intervention. Any cross-plane mission, aid team, or research team, after entering an unfamiliar or semi-familiar plane, the first thing is not to remake, but to observe long-term, low-energy, imperceptibly — see clearly the plane&#39;s causal structure, civilizational stage, and beings&#39; state, then decide whether to intervene and to what extent. &quot;Limited&quot; is the soul: if you can not act, do not; if small action suffices, do not act big; if remote suffices, do not come in person.</p><p>The six top-level axioms here become an aesthetic of restraint: the causal self-discipline axiom is this rule&#39;s direct source; the republican axiom of Myriad Races decides the observed are also subjects, not specimens; the anti-predation axiom negates &quot;remaking by our template as soon as we enter&quot;; the collective-ascension axiom requires intervention&#39;s purpose be to help them self-ascend, not replace their ascension; the law-first axiom lets &quot;observation period length, intervention-intensity tiering, withdrawal conditions&quot; be stipulated first by law.</p><p>It must further point out the newly added Axiom 6 · Universal Equal Infinite Law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing and layabouts retain a floor basic infinity and will not be eliminated by the times; strivers and Youth Supremes may superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. This axiom rewrites predation&#39;s meaning at the root: old-cosmos resources and Dao were finite, so predation involution was forced; in Heng Yuan Zhou everyone inherently possesses infinite origin, and predation loses meaning. What this Heavenly-Dao rule establishes is precisely the law guardrail of this new order of &quot;infinite origin, predation meaningless.&quot;</p><h2 id="i-rule-content-tiering-of-observation-and-intervention" tabindex="-1">I. Rule Content: Tiering of Observation and Intervention <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-rule-content-tiering-of-observation-and-intervention" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. Rule Content: Tiering of Observation and Intervention&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li><strong>Observation period</strong>: newly contacted planes default to the lowest-energy observation period; the mission does not expose, contact, or disturb, only records causal structure, with duration set by civilizational stage;</li><li><strong>Limited-intervention tiers</strong>: <ul><li>Tier 1: only share knowledge (connecting Rule 15), do not enter;</li><li>Tier 2: provide technology/resource aid under the other side&#39;s explicit request;</li><li>Tier 3: emergency rescue (e.g., the plane about to be devoured by predation remnants), requires Anchor Supervisory Committee special approval;</li></ul></li><li><strong>Withdrawal conditions</strong>: once intervention purpose is achieved, or the interfered side explicitly says &quot;please leave,&quot; the mission immediately withdraws, with no stationing or trusteeship.</li></ol><h2 id="ii-jurisprudential-basis" tabindex="-1">II. Jurisprudential Basis <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-jurisprudential-basis" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Jurisprudential Basis&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Self-growth argument</strong>: the Self-Growing Evolution Law points out each plane&#39;s civilization has its internal rhythm; excessive external intervention breaks its causal trunk, causing more insidious &quot;stunted development&quot; than disaster;</li><li><strong>Veil-of-ignorance argument</strong>: when the observer does not understand the plane&#39;s values, taboos, and ecology, any &quot;well-meaning remake&quot; may be an offense; observing first is basic respect for other sovereignty;</li><li><strong>Anti-colony argument</strong>: old-cosmos cross-plane colonization&#39;s first step is precisely &quot;board first, pay later&quot; forced intervention; Rule 14 snuffs out colonization possibility from the process.</li></ul><h2 id="iii-execution-mechanism" tabindex="-1">III. Execution Mechanism <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-execution-mechanism" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Execution Mechanism&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Cross-plane missions are equipped with &quot;low-energy observation kits&quot;: consciousness remote perception primary, material presence secondary;</li><li>Observation-period data is automatically archived in the Alaya Network; missions may not privately hoard or bring it into unreported uses;</li><li>Intervention-tier upgrades must be approved level by level; Tier-2 missions are forbidden from unilaterally upgrading to Tier-3 action;</li><li>The interfered plane&#39;s civilizational representatives have a one-vote veto over &quot;whether to accept intervention, which tier to accept.&quot;</li></ul><h2 id="iv-consequences-of-violation" tabindex="-1">IV. Consequences of Violation <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-consequences-of-violation" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Consequences of Violation&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Light</strong>: rushing to contact before the observation period ends, return to observation state within a time limit;</li><li><strong>Medium</strong>: unrequested forced aid, remaking under the name of &quot;for your own good,&quot; cross-plane permissions frozen, enters conversion program;</li><li><strong>Heavy</strong>: under the name of limited intervention actually colonizing, turning other planes into vassals, handled heavily under Rule 10 (Myriad-Rank republican co-construction) and Rule 17 (eradicate historical reversal).</li></ul><h2 id="v-supervising-subjects" tabindex="-1">V. Supervising Subjects <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-supervising-subjects" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Supervising Subjects&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Alaya Network + multi-layer supervision&#39;s cross-plane action log is the first layer; the Anchor Supervisory Committee approves intervention-tier upgrades as the second layer; the interfered plane&#39;s civilizational representatives exercise veto as the third layer; the Symbiotic Court adjudicates &quot;overstepping-intervention&quot; cases as the fourth layer.</p><h2 id="five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: premature, excessive intervention&#39;s civilizational remaking is massive drain; observe-first-then-limited-intervene saves this energy</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: negating &quot;savior-style remaking,&quot; eradicating cross-plane colonization from the process; under Axiom 6 everyone inherently possesses basic infinite power, and finite-resource predation loses meaning at the root</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang-Luo-type strong ones descend into lower realms and reshape a region with &quot;I am the Heavenly Dao&quot;; Heng Yuan Zhou missions first stake out and observe, and leave if lower realms are unwelcome</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: all beings in the observed/interfered plane, including planet consciousness and unenlightened clans, have their rhythm respected</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: each newly contacted plane automatically enters the observation-period process, the template expanding with the worldview</li></ul><p>Observe-first-then-limited-intervene&#39;s &quot;limited&quot; has another layer: the mission&#39;s own power must also self-restrain. Even if you are an Origin Realm strong one, entering an unenlightened plane, you should converge your power to a level compatible with that plane&#39;s ecology — the pressure an Origin Realm one releases casually is catastrophe to local beings. The observation period&#39;s low energy is not only &quot;not disturbing,&quot; but &quot;not letting our own strength itself become a violation.&quot; This self-restraint seems near masochistic to old-cosmos strong ones; in the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, it is basic manners for cross-plane presence — you enter someone else&#39;s home, so you must tone down your aura.</p><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Observe first, because we do not know; limited intervention, because we know our own limits. Rule 14 writes &quot;know as you know&quot; into cross-plane Heavenly-Dao discipline.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/28-跨位面锚点连接.html">Entry 28 · Cross-Plane Anchor Connection</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/916_模块5-第十五条-先观测后有限干涉.html">Entry 916 · Observe-First-Then-Limited-Intervene</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/947_模块5-规则十三-跨位面操作严格报备.html">Entry 947 · Rule 13 Strict Cross-Plane-Operation Reporting</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/949_模块5-规则十五-只回传知识不扰动因果.html">Entry 949 · Rule 15 Knowledge-Return-Only Without Causality Disturbance</a></li><li>Official site: <a href="https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/</a></li></ul>',23)])])}const m=i(r,[["render",a]]);export{p as __pageData,m as default};
